<title>USA: US Home Builders-Mkt Index revised down in July.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders-Mkt Index revised down in July.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders (NAHB) said its Housing Market Index was revised down to a level of 56 in July, one point lower than the June figure and preliminary July estimate.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, traffic of prospective buyers rose to 45 in July from 44 in June.  </p>
<p>The component index for single-family sales in the next six months fell two points to 59 during the same period.</p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means the number of positive responses received from builders exceeded the number of negative responses. The July index is based on the ratings of 400 respondents. The preliminary index was based on a survey of 124 respondents.</p>
